sec.p:
A commercial tissue microarray comprising 34 paired EC specimens and adjacent-matched noncancerous tissues was obtained from the Wuhan Iwill Biotechnology Company (Wuhan, China) for immunohistochemical analysis. A specific primary antibody against TRIM11 (Abcam, USA) was used for IHC staining. Immunohistochemical scoring was performed independently by two experienced pathologists. Staining intensity was evaluated based on the Fromowitz Standard, and the staining index was calculated using the following formula:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$\mathrm{staining}\;\mathrm{index}=\mathrm{staining}\;\mathrm{intensity}\times\mathrm{percentage}\;\mathrm{of}\;\mathrm{positive}\;\mathrm{cells}$$\end{document}
